meta {
  name: change requisition status
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}requisitions/:id/transition/
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: 2
}

body:json {
  {
    // One of "APPROVED", "ORDERED", "REJECTED", "CANCELLED". Required.
    "status": "APPROVED",

    // Shown in the status history. Optional.
    "note": "Approved from the robot budget"
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Moves a requisition to `APPROVED`, `ORDERED`, `REJECTED` or `CANCELLED`
  (FR-4.3). **Admin only**, except that a requester may cancel their own
  requisition while it's `PENDING`. Each change records the actor, time,
  previous status and note, and is audited. `RECEIVED` goes through "receive
  requisition" so the stock gets added.

  Lifecycle (FR-4.2):
  - `PENDING` -> `APPROVED`, `REJECTED`, `CANCELLED`
  - `APPROVED` -> `ORDERED`, `CANCELLED`
  - `ORDERED` -> `RECEIVED` (through "receive requisition"), `CANCELLED`
  - `RECEIVED`, `REJECTED`, `CANCELLED` are terminal

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "REQ-000002 is now approved.",
    "data": {
      "id": 2,
      "reference": "REQ-000002",
      "component": null,
